    "abstract": "<p>\n                    If\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script upper H\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                            <mml:mi class=\"MJX-tex-caligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">H</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal {H}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is a Hilbert space,\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>A</mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is a positive bounded linear operator on\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script upper H\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                            <mml:mi class=\"MJX-tex-caligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">H</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal {H}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    and\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script upper S\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                            <mml:mi class=\"MJX-tex-caligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">S</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal {S}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is a closed subspace of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script upper H\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                            <mml:mi class=\"MJX-tex-caligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">H</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal {H}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    , the relative position between\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script upper S\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                            <mml:mi class=\"MJX-tex-caligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">S</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal {S}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    and\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A Superscript negative 1 Baseline left-parenthesis script upper S Superscript up-tack Baseline right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mi>A</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  −\n                                  \n                                </mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi class=\"MJX-tex-caligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">S</mml:mi>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                ⊥\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A^{-1}(\\mathcal {S}^\\perp )</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    establishes a notion of compatibility. We show that the compatibility of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left-parenthesis upper A comma script upper S right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>A</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mi class=\"MJX-tex-caligraphic\" mathvariant=\"script\">S</mml:mi>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(A,\\mathcal {S})</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is equivalent to the existence of a convenient orthogonal projection in the operator range\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper R left-parenthesis upper A Superscript 1 slash 2 Baseline right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>R</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:msup>\n                              <mml:mi>A</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                  <mml:mo>/</mml:mo>\n                                </mml:mrow>\n                                <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:mrow>\n                            </mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R(A^{1/2})</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    with its canonical Hilbertian structure.\n                  </p>",
